    "title": "GoodVibe",
    "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.20412229",
    "publication_date": "2026-05-27",
    "description": "<p class=\"text-size-chat leading-[calc(var(--codex-chat-font-size)+8px)] extension:leading-normal my-2\"><strong class=\"font-semibold\">GoodVibe</strong>&nbsp;is the research code repository for the paper&nbsp;<em>GoodVibe</em>, submitted to&nbsp;<strong class=\"font-semibold\">USENIX Security 2026 Cycle 2</strong>. The repository contains the implementation of a neuron-level framework for improving the security of code language models through targeted safety-neuron discovery and selective fine-tuning.</p>\n<p class=\"text-size-chat leading-[calc(var(--codex-chat-font-size)+8px)] extension:leading-normal my-2\">The code supports gradient-based safety-neuron identification, masked neuron fine-tuning, clustered neuron fine-tuning, full-model fine-tuning, LoRA fine-tuning, inference, and safety evaluation with a learned judge. It also includes scripts for running end-to-end experiments and reproducing the main GoodVibe workflow described in the paper.</p>",
